# Data — real files are never committed
data/*.csv
data/*.parquet
data/*.zip

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
*.pyo
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# MLflow (SQLite backend + its artifact store)
mlruns/
mlflow.db
mlflow.db-journal
mlflow.db-wal
mlflow.db-shm

# Trained model artifacts (regenerated by src/train.py, not source-controlled).
#
# `models/*`, not `models/` -- git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY,
# so a negation inside one can never re-include anything. Excluding the
# directory's CONTENTS instead is what lets the exception below actually take
# effect. (`git check-ignore -v models/fairness_audit.json` is the check; with
# `models/` it reported the file ignored and the negation silently did nothing.)
models/*

# ...and the exception. The fairness audit's OUTPUT is source-controlled, and
# the two neighbouring .pkl files are exactly why it has to be.
#
# models/ is gitignored, and so is data/*.csv. So a fresh clone has neither the
# model nor the 167 MB dataset that scripts/audit_fairness.py needs to
# regenerate this file. If it were a build artifact like its neighbours, the
# evidence behind this repo's loudest fairness claim -- Mississippi's EO ratio
# recovering 0.74 -> 0.99 -- would exist only on whichever machine last ran the
# audit, and the README would be asserting it on nobody's authority.
#
# It is ~35 KB of derived aggregate ratios: 50 EO ratios with bootstrap CIs, a
# threshold sweep, an ablation summary. Committing it redistributes no
# applicant data (that is the whole reason data/ is excluded), it makes the
# claim reviewable in a diff, and serving/fairness.py refuses to serve it if
# it ever stops matching the shipped model's trained_at.
!models/fairness_audit.json

# Metaflow local metadata + datastore (regenerated per `flow run`, not source-controlled)
.metaflow/

# Figures are regenerated by notebooks/analysis.ipynb (e.g. the SHAP
# waterfall plot) -- ignore generated contents but keep the placeholder so
# the directory itself still exists after a fresh clone.
figures/*
!figures/.gitkeep

# Claude Code local settings (machine-specific, not project config)
.claude/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
